# chronologia named-period registry — International Chronostratigraphic Chart
#
# Source: ICS International Chronostratigraphic Chart, version 2023/09
#   https://stratigraphy.org/ICSchart/ChronostratChart2023-09.pdf
# Numeric boundary ages: Macrostrat "international intervals" timescale
#   (https://macrostrat.org/api/v2/defs/intervals, CC-BY 4.0), whose ages
#   track the ICS 2023/09 chart (Jurassic 201.4->143.1 Ma, Phanerozoic base
#   538.8 Ma, Holocene base 0.0117 Ma == 11.7 ka all verified against the chart).
# Downloaded: 2026-07-21
#
# CHART VERSION: 2023/09
#
# Ages are in millions of years (Ma) before the Before-Present epoch (AD 1950,
# Stuiver & Polach 1977). Each entry is a chronostratigraphic unit spanning its
# base (b_age, older) down to its top (t_age, younger). Endpoint AstroDate years
# are 1950 - age*1e6, so the span lives on the deep-time BP axis; basis is
# "tabulated". Published GSSP boundary uncertainties (b_unc/t_unc, Ma) are folded
# OUTWARD into the endpoints (start widened to b_age+b_unc, end to t_age-t_unc),
# so the span covers the full published uncertainty envelope. Uncertainties are
# populated for the ratified GSSP boundaries cited in ICS 2023/09 / GTS2020 and
# left 0.0 where the chart states no formal +/- (the mechanism, not exhaustive
# coverage, is what these demonstrate). Parent hierarchy (eon>era>period>epoch>
# age) is derived at load time by containment, not stored.
#
# Format: 7 tab-separated columns:
#   key<TAB>name<TAB>level<TAB>b_age_ma<TAB>t_age_ma<TAB>b_unc_ma<TAB>t_unc_ma
#   level in {eon, era, period, epoch, age}
#
key	name	level	b_age_ma	t_age_ma	b_unc_ma	t_unc_ma
